\details{
\strong{Computation.} The bankfull width \code{Wb} and mean bankfull depth \code{db} define
an equivalent two-segment section with shape parameter
\code{b = (Wb / db) / 100} (McParland et al. 2016, eq. 2; or the value supplied
in \code{b}) and maximum depth \code{dmax = db / (1 - b)}. The water surface is drawn
down below bankfull until the Ferguson (2007) resistance law gives the
target discharge. The resulting mean depth, velocity and Froude number set
the Schweizer et al. (2007) normal/lognormal mixtures of relative depth and
relative velocity, which are integrated into \code{n_bins} bins over relative
values 0 to \code{rel_max}. Depth and velocity suitability are read from the
curves at each bin centre, multiplied, weighted by the joint (independent)
bin probability and summed to a combined suitability \code{CSI};
\verb{WUW = wetted width * CSI} and \code{WUA = reach_length_m * WUW}.

\strong{Returns \code{NULL} with a message} when: any numeric input is missing or not
positive (including \code{discharge_m3s = 0}); \code{gradient_m_per_m >= 1}; the shape
parameter is outside \verb{0 < b < 1}; the discharge exceeds the modelled
bankfull discharge; \code{n_bins < 2}; or an HSI table cannot be prepared.
A warning is issued when \code{gradient_m_per_m > 0.2}, which usually means a
percentage was supplied.

\strong{QA/QC checks.} Every result carries a \code{qaqc} data frame of advisory
TRUE/FALSE checks against the domain in which the method was evaluated
