depth 0.19-3.5 m, D84 55-263 mm, gradient 0.0003-0.04), relative
submergence \code{R / D84 >= 1} and mean depth at the discharge at or above
0.05 m. A failed check never stops the calculation; one consolidated
warning names the failed checks so users can decide whether to proceed.
MAD-based checks are \code{NA} when \code{mad_m3s} is not supplied. See
\code{\link[=qaqc_limits]{qaqc_limits()}}.

\strong{Assumptions} are listed by \code{\link[=model_assumptions]{model_assumptions()}} and stored in the
